# Workload generation

When the user attaches `docs/AI_AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` and asks to generate workloads, follow that file. The chat only needs a `Generate workloads ...` line and, for a VM run, one real `ssh -i <key> root@<IPv4>` line. Extra sentences are optional.

This generator tree is the only template. Do not read or copy any other `TEMPLATE_*` directory. No `Legacy:` line means legacy mode is off. Do not refresh the VM unless the prompt explicitly confirms a refresh.

`through`, `to`, and `-` are inclusive. Repositories are created in the parent of this generator, even when Cursor's open folder is this generator. On the VM they install only under `/opt/benchmarks/<Workload Number>-<Repo Name>`. Do not use `/root` or `/opt/workloads`. Every `run_benchmark.sh` run appends to `/var/opt/benchmarks/runtime_ledger.csv`.

The only generation action is to save the chat text as the submitted-prompt artifact, then run from this generator directory:

```bash
python3 scripts/generation_host_preflight.py --prompt-file ../AI_AGENT_PROMPT_SUBMITTED_<WORKLOADS>_<UTC_TIMESTAMP>.md
```

Then run the start command that preflight prints, exactly as printed. It has this form, with the interpreter preflight chose in place of `<python>`:

```bash
MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 <python> scripts/run_from_prompt.py --prompt-file ../AI_AGENT_PROMPT_SUBMITTED_<WORKLOADS>_<UTC_TIMESTAMP>.md
```

Run both from the generator directory in Git Bash (Windows) or bash. Preflight itself only needs Python 3 to start (`python3`, `python`, or `py -3`). When that interpreter lacks Python 3.10+ or PyYAML, preflight tries `GENERATOR_PYTHON` (if set), then `python3`, `python` and `py -3` on `PATH`, then `/c/Python/python.exe`, `/c/Python3*/python.exe` and `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Python\Python3*\python.exe`, and prints the start command with the first one that has both. If none does, it prints the `pip install pyyaml` command to run first. Do not type `python3` into the start command yourself. `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1` stops Git Bash from rewriting paths. Save the prompt in the project root (the generator's parent) and pass it as the relative `../` path, never a `C:\...` or `/c/...` path.

Do not pass `--remote-root`, `--project-root`, or `--template-root`. Do not reimplement copy, setup, or smoke. Continue until every requested workload is recorded.

A locked overlay is a fingerprint, not a ban. When smoke fails inside a file listed in `results/overlay_lock.json`, write the same bytes in `implementation_components/<component-id>/files/<path>`, the sibling path, and that path's `sha256`, then recheck with `create_one_workload.py --validate-only`. Do not leave the workload failed when those three copies can match. Do not replace the overlay with a new collector. Do not run `create_generated_repo.py` again on a non-empty sibling. `scripts/metric_contract.py` has no lock entry: repair the generator copy and the sibling copy, then use the same recheck. `Locked overlay rewritten` means the sibling and the digest disagree. `Implementation component mismatch` means the sibling and the template source disagree.

Log every change to a generator file during a batch with `python3 scripts/log_generator_repair.py --workload <N> --file <path> --reason "<why>"`. The batch summary ends with that list. A collector reports a counter the host does not have as `na (expected: <reason>)`; do not add new `classify_na` matches.
